.SH NAME
lslc \- Linden Scripting Language compiler and static checker (Mono/LSO)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lslc
.RI [ options ]
.IR file.lsl " [" more.lsl " ...]"
.PP
.B lslc
.B \-c
.RI [ \-o
.IR out.lslbc ]
.IR file.lsl
.PP
.B lslc
.B \-\-list\-builtins
|
.B \-\-list\-builtins\-detailed
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lslc
is the Sakura Studios command-line compiler and static analyser for the
Linden Scripting Language used by Second Life and OpenSimulator.
.PP
By default
.B lslc
performs the same parsing, type checking and semantic analysis that the
official viewer-side LSL compiler does, but with substantially richer
diagnostics (carets, hints, source context, categorisation) and without
needing a running viewer. It targets either the modern
.B Mono
runtime (the default, with a 64 KiB per-script memory budget) or the
legacy
.B LSO
virtual machine (16 KiB budget; rejects Mono-only built-ins such as
.BR llJson* ,
.BR llLinksetData* ,
.BR llCastRay ,
.BR llChar ,
.BR llOrd ,
.BR llHMAC ,
and
.BR llTransferLindenDollars ).
.PP
With
.B \-c
.B lslc
additionally emits a portable SLBC bytecode file (extension
.IR .lslbc )
suitable for execution under
.BR slemu (1)
or interactive debugging with
.BR lsldb (1).
.PP
The driver also includes a small
.BR cpp -style
preprocessor with
.BR \-I ,
.BR \-D
and
.B #include
support, so larger projects can be split into headers and modules without
losing single-file-script compatibility on upload.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Targeting
.TP
.B \-\-mono
Target the Mono virtual machine (default). The per-script memory budget
is set to 64 KiB.
.TP
.B \-\-lso
Target the legacy LSO virtual machine. The per-script budget is
16 KiB and Mono-only built-ins are rejected at compile time.
.TP
.BI \-\-memory\-budget= N
Override the per-script memory budget, in bytes. A value of
.B 0
behaves like
.BR \-\-no\-memory\-check .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-memory\-check
Disable source-size based budget warnings and errors.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-wall ", " \-Wall
Enable extra warnings (unused variables, shadowed parameters,
suspicious casts, etc.).
.TP
.B \-Werror
Treat all warnings as errors.
.TP
.B \-fsyntax\-only
Only run syntax and type checking. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-fno\-color
Suppress ANSI colour escapes in diagnostics, even when stderr is a TTY.
.TP
.BI \-fmax\-errors= N
Stop emitting after
.I N
errors. The default is
.BR 50 .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only a one-line summary per file on errors; suppress source
carets.
.SS Preprocessor
.TP
.BI \-I " PATH"
Add
.I PATH
to the
.B #include
search list. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-D " NAME" [= value ]
Pre-define a macro, as with
.BR cpp (1).
.TP
.B \-E
Run only the preprocessor; write the preprocessed source to standard
output and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-preprocess
Skip the preprocessor entirely. The source is fed straight to the
lexer.
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-emit\-bytecode
Emit SLBC bytecode (.lslbc) consumable by
.BR slemu (1).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
With
.BR \-c ,
write the bytecode to
.IR FILE .
The default is the input path with the extension replaced by
.BR .lslbc .
.TP
.BI \-\-diag\-output " FILE"
Redirect all diagnostics to
.I FILE
instead of standard error.
.SS Informational
.TP
.B \-\-list\-builtins
Print every built-in function, constant and event name known to
.BR lslc ,
one per line, grouped by category.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-builtins\-detailed
Print a stable JSON-line dump of every built-in function, constant and
event, including return types, parameter types and parameter names.
Designed for consumption by IDE tooling such as
.BR sakura-intellij-lsl .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the
.B lslc
version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Stop option parsing; all following arguments are treated as input
files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Compile a single script under the default Mono target. On success a
short
.B "OK"
line is printed for each file; on failure
.B lslc
exits non-zero and prints categorised diagnostics:
.PP
.RS
.B lslc greeter.lsl
.RE
.PP
Produce SLBC bytecode for
.BR slemu (1)
or
.BR lsldb (1).
Without
.BR \-o ,
the output is written next to the input with the
.B .lslbc
extension:
.PP
.RS
.B lslc \-c greeter.lsl
.br
.B lslc \-c \-o build/greeter.lslbc src/greeter.lsl
.RE
.PP
Enable all extra warnings and fail the build on any of them \(em
recommended in CI:
.PP
.RS
.B lslc \-Wall \-Werror src/*.lsl
.RE
.PP
Lint a script against the legacy LSO virtual machine before uploading
to an OpenSim region that has not enabled Mono. Mono-only built-ins are
reported as errors, and the memory budget is reduced to 16 KiB:
.PP
.RS
.B lslc \-\-lso \-Wall legacy_hud.lsl
.RE
.PP
Enumerate the built-in library available to scripts \(em useful when
writing a syntax highlighter or completion provider:
.PP
.RS
.B lslc \-\-list\-builtins\-detailed | head
.RE
.PP
Use the preprocessor to share constants between several scripts.
Headers are resolved against every
.B \-I
directory in the order they were given on the command line:
.PP
.RS
.B lslc \-Iinclude \-DDEBUG=1 \-DOWNER_KEY=\(dq...\(dq vendor.lsl
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All input files compiled and type-checked successfully (zero errors).
Warnings may have been emitted unless
.B \-Werror
was given.
.TP
.B 1
At least one input file failed to compile, or bytecode emission failed.
.TP
.B 2
Internal driver error: bad command line, out of memory, unreadable
input, or an unwriteable
.B \-o
target.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR file .lsl
LSL source file. May contain preprocessor directives.
.TP
.IR file .lslbc
SLBC bytecode emitted by
.B lslc \-c
and consumed by
.BR slemu (1)
and
.BR lsldb (1).
.TP
.I ./
The current directory and every
.B \-I
directory are searched for
.B #include
headers.
.SH BUGS
The memory-budget check is a source-size heuristic (comments and
whitespace stripped); it tracks the official viewer's
.RB \(lq "estimated bytecode size" \(rq
widget closely but is not exact. A script that
.B lslc
accepts as within budget may still be rejected at upload time if its
compiled string table or initialiser data is unusually large.
.PP
Please report bugs to
.MT shiho@sakurastudios.eu
Shiho Sakura
